    "plan_update_summary": "### Cycle #50 Post-Mortem & Parameter Mutation\nForensic analysis of Cycle #50 revealed that the strategy was actually gross-profitable (+\u20b910.58) in Out-of-Sample testing, but turned net-negative (-\u20b924.11) solely due to \u20b934.69 in statutory fees and brokerage drag across 9 trades. Specifically, `TATASTEEL` suffered repeated stop-outs around ~0.63% adverse excursions during mid-morning liquidity sweeps, while `ICICIBANK` and afternoon setups decayed into fee-losing scratch trades via premature `0.95R` trailing stops and `EOD_SQUARE_OFF` exits. To resolve this, we are widening `min_sl_pct` from `0.55%` to `0.68%` to survive standard 5m order-book noise, delaying `breakeven_trigger_r` from `0.95R` to `1.15R` to give trades room to breathe while ensuring fee coverage, slightly tightening `min_target_pct` to `1.05%` so afternoon setups can clear targets before the 15:15 IST square-off window, and maximizing `min_sweep_vol_multiplier` to `3.00x` to filter out low-conviction mid-day fakeouts."
